g to the processing fee\"* — instead of a chain of near-identical conditionals.\n- **Rule 3 (DRY):** Each premium value now has a **single representation** (`sword: 115`), and the repeated `if (itemType === X) return Y` pattern is gone. Adding the next type (potion=49) is a one-line table entry instead of a new constant + a new `if`.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest elements):** 4 constants + 3 conditionals + function → 1 table + 1 function with 2 nullish-coalescings; fewer elements overall.\n\nThe `PROCESSING_FEE` constant is retained because it serves as the named fallback (not tied to a key), preserving clarity where a bare `5` would be a magic number.\n\n### Done\n**Refactoring**: lookup table replaces if-chain + per-type constants.\n**Mass change**: 54 → 33 (−21).\n**Tests**: all passing (4/4); `office.ts` type-checks clean."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-48-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_glm-5-2/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/office.ts\nPassing tests: 4\nRecent Green phase: Added a `staff` branch (STAFF_PREMIUM=93) to premiumForItemType. Pattern: sword->115, amulet->71, staff->93, else fee-only 5.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/office.ts\nPassing tests: 4\nRecent Green phase: Added a `staff` branch (STAFF_PREMIUM=93) to premiumForItemType. Pattern: sword->115, amulet->71, staff->93, else fee-only 5.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784951796459},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the implementation file and test fi