ring[]` type-cast workaround in favor of idiomatic `Set.has(...)` is a net clarity win. Behavior is identical (membership test over the same two types).\n\n### Step 6: Decision Documentation\n\n**Refactoring Applied:**\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent):** Replaced `[\"rune\",\"moonstone\"] as const` + `(COMPONENT_TYPES as readonly string[]).includes(type)` with `new Set([...])` + `COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type)`. This removes a TypeScript type-narrowing workaround that obscured the simple membership check. `Set.has` is the idiomatic, cast-free way to express \"is this type in the fixed component group.\"\n- **Mass:** 20 → 22 (+2), accepted because clarity (Rule 2) takes priority over mass.\n- **Naming:** Evaluated all functions (`policyBasePremium`, `isComponent`, `roundUp`, `runScenario`) — each already clearly reveals its intent. No renames.\n\n**Considered and rejected:**\n- Extracting a `componentPremium(count)` helper for the block ternary — mass increases (25→29) and adds an element; the inline ternary with named constants (`BLOCK_SIZE`, `BLOCK_PREMIUM`, `COMPONENT_BASE`) already reveals intent.\n- Inlining `isComponent` — reduces mass but the named predicate reads more naturally at the call site; Rule 2 favored keeping it.\n\n### Step 7: Completion\n\n**Refactoring:** Replaced array+cast membership check with idiomatic `Set.has` (Rule 2 clarity win).\n**Mass Change:** 20 → 22 (+2, justified by Rule 2 over APP).\n**Tests:** All 7 passing (31 todo)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-48-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_glm-5-2/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/office.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: Added component block logic — components grouped by type; a group of exactly 3 alike costs BLOCK_PREMIUM=60, otherwise count*COMPONENT_BASE(25). Main items still use BASE_PREMIUM table. policyBasePremium(items) sums it all.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/office.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: Added component block logic — components grouped by type; a group of exactly 3 alike costs BLOCK_PREMIUM=60, otherwise count*COMPONENT_BASE(25). Main items still use BASE_PREMIUM table. policyBasePremium(items) sums it all.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784952143483},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by understanding the current state of the code. I need to read the implementation file and the test file to understand what I'm working with.\n\nLet me read both files first.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_406b32db72494c27ae2631dd","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5398315cdefc4db3bfd3cade","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":88,"output":66,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":39,"totalTokens":6170,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784952143503,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-673be46e-a447-4785-9e83-f5ef4c3a8dc4","responseModel":"z-ai/glm-5.2"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_406b32db72494c27ae2631dd","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// MHPCO Claim Office — scenario processing.\n\nexport type QuoteResult = { premium: number };\nexport type ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n\n/** Absorb floating-point noise before applying the MHPCO's whole-G rounding. */\nconst EPSILON = 1e-9;\nconst roundUp = (amount: number): number => Math.ceil(amount - EPSILON);\n\n/** Base premium per single main item type. */\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Partial<Record<string, number>> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\n/** Components are insured at a flat per-item value; a block of 3 alike is offered cheaper. */\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"] as const;\nconst COMPONENT_BASE = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean =>\n  (COMPONENT_TYPES as readonly string[]).includes(type);\n\n/** Summed base premium of all quoted items, applying the 3-alike-component block. */\nfunction policyBasePremium(items: Array<{ type: string }>): number {\n  let total = 0;\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (isComponent(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      total += BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    }\n  }\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    total += count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n  }\n  return total;\n}\n\n/** Input shape for `runScenario`: a list of steps, each optionally carrying typed items. */\ntype Scenario = { steps: Array<{ op: string; items?: Array<{ type: string }> }> };\n\nexport function runScenario(input: unknown): { results: StepResult[] } {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  const step = scenario.steps[0];\n  const items = step.items ?? [];\n  const policyBase = policyBasePremium(items);\n  const premium = roundUp(policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE) + PROCESSING_FEE);\n  return { results: [{ premium }] };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784952144476},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5398315cdefc4db3bfd3cade","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { resolve } from \"node:path\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./office.js\";\n\n/** Run the CLI as a subprocess, feeding `input` as stdin JSON. */\nfunction runCli(input: unknown): { stdout: string; stderr: string; exitCode: number } {\n  const cliPath = resolve(process.cwd(), \"src/cli.ts\");\n  const bin = resolve(process.cwd(), \"node_modules/.bin/tsx\");\n  try {\n    const stdout = execFileSync(bin, [cliPath], {\n      input: JSON.stringify(input),\n      encoding: \"utf-8\",\n      timeout: 30000,\n    });\n    return { stdout, stderr: \"\", exitCode: 0 };\n  } catch (err) {\n    const e = err as { stdout?: string; stderr?: string; status?: number };\n    return {\n      stdout: e.stdout ?? \"\",\n      stderr: e.stderr ?? \"\",\n      exitCode: e.status ?? 1,\n    };\n  }\n}\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  it(\"quote: empty item list -> premium 5 (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single sword -> premium 115\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single amulet -> premium 71\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single staff -> premium 93\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 93 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single potion -> premium 49\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 49 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: 2 runes -> premium 60\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: 3 runes (block applies) -> premium 71\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"quote: 4 runes (no block) -> premium 115\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: 7 runes -> premium 198 (ceil 197.5)\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: 2 runes + 1 moonstone (no block) -> premium 88 (ceil 87.5)\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: 3 runes + 3 moonstones (two blocks) -> premium 137\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: cursed sword newcomer -> premium 165\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: high-enchanted sword enchant 5 -> premium 145\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: sword enchant 4 (no high enchant) -> premium 115\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: cursed sword enchant 5 (both surcharges) -> premium 195\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: loyalty at exactly 2 years -> premium 95\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: follow-up contract (2nd quote) sword -> 1st 115, 2nd 100\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: cursed sword + plain amulet scope -> premium 231\");\n  it.todo(\"quote: long-standing 2nd contract cursed enchant 7 -> 1st 95, 2nd 160\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: standard sword enchant 3 damage 500 -> payout 400, cap 1600\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: rune damage 200 -> payout 100, cap 400\");\n  