model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":192,"output":50,"cacheRead":22080,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":25,"totalTokens":22322,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784952336448,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-96cba85c-4c47-4a60-b7c1-ae041d71c05f","responseModel":"z-ai/glm-5.2"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_19cdcc1de2974c71a1ac29de","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// MHPCO Claim Office — scenario processing.\n\nexport type QuoteResult = { premium: number };\nexport type ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_RATE = 0.5;\n\n/** Absorb floating-point noise before applying the MHPCO's whole-G rounding. */\nconst EPSILON = 1e-9;\nconst roundUp = (amount: number): number => Math.ceil(amount - EPSILON);\n\n/** A quoted item: type plus optional magical attributes. */\ntype Item = { type: string; material?: string; enchantment?: number; cursed?: boolean };\n\n/** Base premium per single main item type. */\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Partial<Record<string, number>> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\n/** Components are insured at a flat per-item value; a block of 3 alike is offered cheaper. */\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst COMPONENT_BASE = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type);\n\n/** Summed base premium of all quoted items, applying the 3-alike-component block. */\nfunction policyBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  let total = 0;\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (isComponent(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      total += itemBaseValue(item);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    total += count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n  }\n  return total;\n}\n\n/** Per-item base value: a single item's premium, before block discounts. */\nfunction itemBaseValue(item: Item): number {\n  return isComponent(item.type) ? COMPONENT_BASE : BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n}\n\n/** Item-specific risk surcharges (cursed). Applied to the affected item's base premium. */\nfunction itemSurcharges(item: Item): number {\n  return item.cursed ? CURSE_RATE * itemBaseValue(item) : 0;\n}\n\n/** Input shape for `runScenario`: a list of steps, each optionally carrying typed items. */\ntype Scenario = { steps: Array<{ op: string; items?: Item[] }> };\n\nexport function runScenario(input: unknown): { results: StepResult[] } {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  const step = scenario.steps[0];\n  const items = step.items ?? [];\n  const policyBase = policyBasePremium(items);\n  const surcharges = items.reduce((sum, it) => sum + itemSurcharges(it), 0);\n  const firstInsurance = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\n  const premium = roundUp(policyBase + surcharges + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE);\n  return { results: [{ premium }] };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784952337360},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Everything looks good. Let me write up the final report.\n\nLet me compute the mass changes:\n\n**`itemSurcharges` mass:**\nBefore:\n- `let surcharge = 0`: assignment(6) + binding(1) + const(1) = 8\n- `if (item.cursed)`: conditional(4) + binding(item)(1) = 5\n- `surcharge += CURSE_RATE * itemBaseValue(item)`: assignment(6) + binding(surcharge)(1) + binding(CURSE_RATE)(1) + invocation(itemBaseValue)(2) + binding(item)(1) = 11\n- `return surcharge`: binding(1) = 1\n- function signature binding (item): 1\nTotal ≈ 26\n\nAfter (ternary):\n- `return item.cursed ? CURSE_RATE * itemBaseValue(item) : 0`: binding(item)(1) + conditional(?:)(4) + binding(CURSE_RATE)(1) + invocation(itemBaseValue)(2) + binding(item)(1) + const(0)(1) = 10\n- function signature binding (item): 1\nTotal ≈ 11\n\nDelta: -15\n\n**`policyBasePremium` non-component branch mass:**\nBefore: `total += BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0`: assignment(6) + binding(total)(1) + binding(BASE_PREMIUM)(1) + binding(item)(1) + conditional(??)(4) + const(0)(1) = 14\nAfter: `total += itemBaseValue(item)`: assignment(6) + binding(total)(1) + invocation(itemBaseValue)(2) + binding(item)(1) = 10\nDelta: -4\n\nTotal mass change: -19.\n\nAlso, the `BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0` knowledge is now in a single place (itemBaseValue), removing duplication.\n\nLet me write the final report.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Both refactorings complete and all tests green. Here is the summary.\n\n## Refactoring Report\n\n### Refactorings Applied\n\n**1. DRY — consolidate base-value knowledge (Rule 3)**\n\n`BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0` appeared in *two* places: `policyBasePremium`'s non-component branch and `itemBaseValue`. Since `itemBaseValue(item)` already returns exactly that value for non-components, `policyBasePremium` now delegates to it. `itemBaseValue` is the single source of truth for \"an item's base value\"; the `?? 0` defaulting rule lives in one spot. Its doc comment was broadened from \"used for item-specific surcharges\" to \"a single item's premium, before block discounts\" to reflect its broader role.\n\n**2. Simplify `itemSurcharges` to a direct ternary (Rule 2 + Rule 4)**\n\nThe `let surcharge = 0; if (item.cursed) surcharge += …; return surcharge;` accumulation pattern is speculative structure — there is currently only *one* surcharge source. A ternary accurately reveals the present single-condition intent and drops a mutation and a binding. (When the upcoming enchantment-surcharge test arrives, the Green phase will adapt; we refactor for current tests, not anticipated ones.)\n\n### APP Mass\n\n`itemSurcharges`:\n- Befor