"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Green Phase Complete: Added loyalty discount (−20% of policy base when years ≥ 2). 16 passing. Proceeding to Refactor."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f8823a50abf142078d332f93","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/office.ts\nPassing tests: 16\nRecent Green phase: Added LOYALTY_RATE=0.2 discount (policy-wide, -20% of policy base) when customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD(2). Extended Scenario type with customer:{yearsWithMHPCO}.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":1914,"output":154,"cacheRead":91712,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1,"totalTokens":93780,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784952458870,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d84a5ff0-1cf6-4d8c-877e-9db2a8d96b9b","responseModel":"z-ai/glm-5.2"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f8823a50abf142078d332f93","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 16 tests pass and lint is clean.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring Applied**: Naming + intent (Rule 2) — renamed `loyalty` → `loyaltyDiscount`, stored as a **positive** discount amount and **subtracted** explicitly in the premium sum, instead of a negative value silently added.\n\n### Mass Calculation (changed region)\n\n**Before** (`22`):\n```typescript\nconst loyalty = ... ? -LOYALTY_RATE * policyBase : 0;\nconst premium = roundUp(policyBase + surcharges + firstInsurance + loyalty + PROCESSING_FEE);\n```\n- Bindings: `loyalty` (1) · Constants: `0` (1)\n- Invocations: `>=`(2), unary `-`(2), `*`(2), `+`×4(8), `roundUp`(2) = 16\n- Conditionals: `?:` (4) → **Total: 22**\n\n**After** (`20`):\n```typescript\nconst loyaltyDiscount = ... ? LOYALTY_RATE * policyBase : 0;\nconst premium = roundUp(\n  policyBase + surcharges + firstInsurance - loyaltyDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE,\n);\n```\n- Bindings: `loyaltyDiscount` (1) · Constants: `0` (1)\n- Invocations: `>=`(2), `*`(2), `+`×3(6), `-`(2), `roundUp`(2) = 14\n- Conditionals: `?:` (4) → **Total: 20**\n\n**Mass Change**: 22 → 20 (Δ −2, removed the unary negation operator). The larger win is clarity: the premium line now reads like a receipt — `base + surcharges + firstInsurance − loyaltyDiscount + fee`.\n\n### Simple Design Evaluation\n\n| Rule | Result |\n|------|--------|\n| **1. Tests Pass** | ✅ 16 passing, lint clean |\n| **2. Reveals Intent** | ✅ Improved — `loyaltyDiscount` is a positive amount, explicitly subtracted; sign is no longer a hidden implementation detail |\n| **3. No Duplication** | No duplication introduced; none found to remove |\n| **4. Fewest Elements** | No new elements; removed one operator (unary `-`) |\n\n### Other refactorings considered but rejected\n- **`itemSurcharges` `let`/`+=` → ternary sum**: current accumulate form is idiomatic and clear; ternary rewrite would lengthen lines without a clear Rule 2 gain.\n- **Extract `loyaltyDiscountFor()` helper**: would add an element (Rule 4) for a one-line ternary already clear inline — over-engineering.\n- **Rename `firstInsurance` → `firstInsuranceSurcharge`**: marginal parallelism, but lengthens the premium line toward a readability-damaging wrap; `firstInsurance` is the domain concept and is unambiguously additive in context.\n- **Remove unused `ClaimResult`/`StepResult` types**: they document the claims domain contract (forward-looking for the many `it.todo` claim tests); Rule 2 intent justifies keeping them over Rule 4.\n\n**Tests**: All 16 passing."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-48-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_glm-5-2/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/office.ts\nPassing tests: 16\nRecent Green phase: Added LOYALTY_RATE=0.2 discount (policy-wide, -20% of policy base) when customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD(2). Extended Scenario type with customer:{yearsWithMHPCO}.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/office.ts\nPassing tests: 16\nRecent Green phase: Added LOYALTY_RATE=0.2 discount (policy-wide, -20% of policy base) when customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD(2). Extended Scenario type with customer:{yearsWithMHPCO}.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784952462431},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the test file and implementation file to understand what we're working with.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll refactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Let me start by examining the current state of both files."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8eb4f2dc5c474049afc40c13","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1936ff0c787d42e8a3e0e2b7","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":87,"output":70,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":20,"totalTokens":6173,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784952462458,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-680ef704-54fb-4e1f-b760-2e6ab686cd35","responseModel":"z-ai/glm-5.2"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8eb4f2dc5c474049afc40c13","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// MHPCO Claim Office — scenario processing.\n\nexport type QuoteResult = { premium: number };\nexport type ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANT_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst LOYALTY_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD = 2;\n\n/** Absorb floating-point noise before applying the MHPCO's whole-G rounding. */\nconst EPSILON = 1e-9;\nconst roundUp = (amount: number): number => Math.ceil(amount - EPSILON);\n\n/** A quoted item: type plus optional magical attributes. */\ntype Item = { type: string; material?: string; enchantment?: number; cursed?: boolean };\n\n/** Base premium per single main item type. */\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Partial<Record<string, number>> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\n/** Components are insured at a flat per-item value; a block of 3 alike is offered cheaper. */\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst COMPONENT_BASE = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type);\n\n/** Summed base premium of all quoted items, applying the 3-alike-component block. */\nfunction policyBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  let total = 0;\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (isComponent(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      total += itemBaseValue(item);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    total += count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n  }\n  return total;\n}\n\n/** Per-item base value: a single item's premium, before block discounts. */\nfunction itemBaseValue(item: Item): number {\n  return isComponent(item.type) ? COMPONENT_BASE : BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n}\n\n/** Item-specific risk surcharges (cursed, high enchantment). Applied to the affected item's base premium. */\nfunction itemSurcharges(item: Item): number {\n  const base = itemBaseValue(item);\n  let surcharge = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) surcharge += CURSE_RATE * base;\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANT_THRESHOLD) surcharge += HIGH_ENCHANT_RATE * base;\n  return surcharge;\n}\n\n/** Input shape for `runScenario`: a single customer and a list of steps. */\ntype Scenario = {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Array<{ op: string; items?: Item[] }>;\n};\n\nexport function runScenario(input: unknown): { results: StepResult[] } {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  const step = scenario.steps[0];\n  const items = step.items ?? [];\n  const policyBase = policyBasePremium(items);\n  const surcharges = items.reduce((sum, it) => sum + itemSurcharges(it), 0);\n  const firstInsurance = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\n  const loyalty =\n    scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD\n      ? -LOYALTY_RATE * policyBase\n      : 0;\n  const premium = roundUp(policyBase + surcharges + firstInsurance + loyalty + PROCESSING_FEE);\n  return { results: [{ premium }] };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784952463269},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1936ff0c787d42e8a3e0e2b7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { resolve } from \"node:path\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./office.js\";\n\n/** Run the CLI as a subprocess, feeding `input` as stdin JSON. */\nfunction runCli(input: unknown): { stdout: string; stderr: string; exitCode: number } {\n  const cliPath = resolve(process.cwd(), \"src/cli.ts\");\n  const bin = resolve(process.cwd(), \"node_modules/.bin/tsx\");\n  try {\n    const stdout = execFileSync(bin, [cliPath], {\n      input: JSON.stringify(input),\n      encoding: \"utf-8\",\n      timeout: 30000,\n    });\n    return { stdout, stderr: \"\", exitCode: 0 };\n  } catch (err) {\n    const e = err as { stdout?: string; stderr?: string; status?: number };\n    return {\n      stdout: e.stdout ?? \"\",\n      stderr: e.stderr ?? \"\",\n      exitCode: e.status ?? 1,\n    };\n  }\n}\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  it(\"quote: empty item list -> premium 5 (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single sword -> premium 115\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single amulet -> premium 71\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single staff -> premium 93\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 93 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single potion -> premium 49\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 49 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: 2 runes -> premium 60\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: 3 ru