t`, `result`)\n- **Invocation** (Mass: 2): Function calls (`calculate()`, `Math.max()`)\n- **Conditional** (Mass: 4): Control flow (`if`, `switch`, `?:`)\n- **Loop** (Mass: 5): Iteration (`for`, `forEach`, `map`)\n- **Assignment** (Mass: 6): Mutations (`x = 5`, `count++`)\n\nLet me focus on the function most recently changed - `quotePremium` and `runScenario`, since those are the ones touched in the last Green phase.\n\n```typescript\nfunction quotePremium(\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number },\n  items: Item[],\n  isFollowUp: boolean,\n): number {\n  const policyBase = policyBasePremium(items);\n  const surcharges = items.reduce((sum, it) => sum + itemSurcharges(it), 0);\n  const firstInsurance = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD ? LOYALTY_RATE * policyBase : 0;\n  const followUpDiscount = isFollowUp ? FOLLOW_UP_RATE * policyBase : 0;\n  return roundUp(\n    policyBase + surcharges + firstInsurance - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE,\n  );\n}\n```\n\nLet me count mass for `quotePremium`:\n- Bindings (params): customer, items, isFollowUp = 3\n- Constants: 0 (FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE etc. are module-level, but here `0` literals in ternaries = 2 constants)\n- `policyBasePremium(items)` invocation = 2\n- assignment to policyBase = 6\n- binding policyBase = 1\n- `items.reduce(...)` invocation = 2\n- `0` constant = 1\n- loop (reduce is iteration) = 5\n- bindings sum, it = 2\n- `itemSurcharges(it)` invocation = 2\n- `sum + itemSurcharges(it)` -- addition? Is `+` an invocation? In the example, `+` was counted as an invocation (mass 2). Hmm, let me re-read.\n\nLooking at the example:\n```\nfunction calculate(numbers: number[]): number {\n  return numbers.reduce((sum, num) => sum + num, 0);\n}\n\nComponent Count:\n- Constants: 1 (literal 0) = 1\n- Bindings: 3 (numbers, sum, num) = 3\n- Invocations: 2 (reduce, +) = 4\n- Conditionals: 0 = 0\n- Loops: 1 (reduce is iteration) = 5\n- A