ndent. Let me match. The `results.push({ premium: quotePremium(...) });` was on one line. My new version breaks it across lines because `hasPriorQuote` makes the line a bit longer. Let me check line length:\n`      results.push({ premium: quotePremium(scenario.customer, step.items ?? [], hasPriorQuote) });`\nThat's 6 + len(\"results.push({ premium: quotePremium(scenario.customer, step.items ?? [], hasPriorQuote) });\"). Let me count: \"results.push({ premium: quotePremium(scenario.customer, step.items ?? [], hasPriorQuote) });\" = ~88 chars + 6 indent = 94. That might exceed a prettier line-width (usually 80). Let me keep it broken across lines to be safe, OR check if there's a prettier config.\n\nLet me check for a prettier/eslint config.\n\nActually, let me just keep the multi-line format to be safe and readable. But let me verify the project's formatting expectations by checking if there's a prettier config and running format check after.\n\nLet me make the edit and then run tests + format check.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"All 17 tests pass. Let me examine the project structure and formatting conventions before refactoring."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_eaba3f89ad344c1aa30a6534","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -a && echo \"---PRETTIER---\" && cat .prettierrc* 2>/dev/null; cat package.json 2>/dev/null | head -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":220,"output":8020,"cacheRead":9536,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7955,"totalTokens":17776,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784952597854,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-20629bb8-5cc9-43ee-99f1-0b9ee77adf62","responseModel":"z-ai/glm-5.2"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_eaba3f89ad344c1aa30a6534","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":".\n..\n.pi\nAGENTS.md\neslint.config.mjs\nmetrics.json\nnode_modules\npackage.json\npnpm-lock.yaml\n