e test 21 and write it carefully.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the premium for 1 rune: policyBase = 25 (1 rune, no block). first = 2.5. fee 5. = 32.5 → 33. Yes.\n\nLet me write test 21.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Green Phase Complete: Implemented claim processing — policy cap (2×insurance sum), damage matching, reimbursement rate, per-damage deductible, sum+floor+cap. 20 passing. Proceeding to Refactor."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_10787cb6cc65405fa19e0922","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/office.ts\nPassing tests: 20\nRecent Green phase: Implemented claim processing. Added INSURANCE_VALUE table (sword1000/amulet600/staff800/potion400, components 250), insuranceSum(), a Policy type {items, remainingCap}, reimbursementRate() (0.5 if enchantment>=8 else 1.0), processClaim() which matches damages to policy items (splice from a pool, throws if not found), applies a 100 G deductible per damage, sums, floors (roundDown), and caps at remainingCap. runScenario now stores policies by step index and dispatches claim steps. Added roundDown helper.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":80,"output":576,"cacheRead":109056,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":343,"totalTokens":109712,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784952746415,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-c9eee73d-202b-4a7e-a0c6-7e64bdeef12e","responseModel":"z-ai/glm-5.2"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_10787cb6cc65405fa19e0922","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 5: New APP Mass\n\nThe rename `desired` → `uncappedPayout` is a binding→binding rename (mass 1 → 1) at all three use sites. No new elements added, none removed.\n\n**Refactored total (affected region): 103** (unchanged)\n\n**Mass Change: 103 → 103 (Δ 0)**\n\nThis is expected and acceptable: the improvement is purely **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**, which explicitly trumps APP per the guidelines.\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- **Naming (Rule 2)**: Renamed `desired` → `uncappedPayout` in `processClaim`. The old name was vague (\"desired what?\"); the new name precisely describes the value's role — the payout total *before* `remainingCap` is applied — and reads naturally at the capping line `Math.min(uncappedPayout, policy.remainingCap)`.\n\n**Considered and rejected** (with mass reasoning):\n- Consolidate `itemBaseValue`/`itemInsuranceValue` into a generic `itemValue(item, flat, table)` — rejected: +4 mass, adds a 3-param abstraction for two clear 1-liners (hurts Rule 4 & readability).\n- Extract `reimbursementFor(item, amount)` helper — rejected: the inline `rate * amount - DEDUCTIBLE` *is* the visible business rule; hiding it costs +6 mass and forces a jump.\n- Extract `itemEnchantment(item) = item.enchantment ?? 0` (used twice) — rejected: +mass for a tiny idiom.\n- Name the magic `1` in `reimbursementRate` as `FULL_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE` — rejected: the doc comment already says \"else full\", `1` is universally understood, and a single-use constant adds +8 mass for no real clarity gain.\n\n**Benefits**:\n- `processClaim` now reads: accumulate `uncappedPayout`, then `payout = roundDown(min(uncappedPayout, remainingCap))` — the cap semantics are self-documenting.\n- Zero risk, zero mass penalty, no new abstractions.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n- **Refactoring**: Renamed `desired` → `uncappedPayout` (Rule 2: Reveals Intent) in `processClaim`.\n- **Mass Change**: 103 → 103 (Δ 0) — intent improvement, APP neutral (Rule 2 trumps APP).\n- **Tests**: All 20 passing (18 still `.todo`)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-48-17_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_glm-5-2/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/office.ts\nPassing tests: 20\nRecent Green phase: Implemented claim processing. Added INSURANCE_VALUE table (sword1000/amulet600/staff800/potion400, components 250), insuranceSum(), a Policy type {items, remainingCap}, reimbursementRate() (0.5 if enchantment>=8 else 1.0), processClaim() which matches damages to policy items (splice from a pool, throws if not found), applies a 100 G deductible per damage, sums, floors (roundDown), and caps at remainingCap. runScenario now stores policies by step index and dispatches claim steps. Added roundDown helper.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/office.ts\nPassing tests: 20\nRecent Green phase: Implemented claim processing. Added INSURANCE_VALUE table (sword1000/amulet600/staff800/potion400, components 250), insuranceSum(), a Policy type {items, remainingCap}, reimbursementRate() (0.5 if enchantment>=8 else 1.0), processClaim() which matches damages to policy items (splice from a pool, throws if not found), applies a 100 G deductible per damage, sums, floors (roundDown), and caps at remainingCap. runScenario now stores policies by step index and dispatches claim steps. Added roundDown helper.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784952753452},{"role":"assistant","content":[],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"error","timestamp":1784952753478,"errorMessage":"Request timed out."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by examining the current state of the implementation and test files to understand what I'm working with.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c30652eec3514bc8a294c489","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ef9554dd4f47463a82b21202","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":154,"output":50,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":23,"totalTokens":6220,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784953055490,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3215b1a1-8a3c-47c3-a414-cdcfe87bffeb","responseModel":"z-ai/glm-5.2"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c30652eec3514bc8a294c489","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// MHPCO Claim Office — scenario processing.\n\nexport type QuoteResult = { premium: number };\nexport type ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANT_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst LOYALTY_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_RATE = 0.15;\n\n/** Claim processing. */\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANT_CLAIM_RATE = 0.5;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\n/** Absorb floating-point noise before applying the MHPCO's whole-G rounding. */\nconst EPSILON = 1e-9;\nconst roundUp = (amount: number): number => Math.ceil(amount - EPSILON);\nconst roundDown = (amount: number): number => Math.floor(amount + EPSILON);\n\n/** A quoted item: type plus optional magical attributes. */\ntype Item = { type: string; material?: string; enchantment?: number; cursed?: boolean };\n\n/** Base premium per single main item type. */\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Partial<Record<string, number>> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\n/** Insurance value per single main item type; components are 250 G each. */\nconst INSURANCE_VALUE: Partial<Record<string, number>> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n};\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 250;\n\n/** Components are insured at a flat per-item value; a block of 3 alike is offered cheaper. */\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst COMPONENT_BASE = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type);\n\n/** Summed base premium of all quoted items, applying the 3-alike-component block. */\nfunction policyBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  let total = 0;\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (isComponent(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      total += itemBaseValue(item);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    total += count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n  }\n  return total;\n}\n\n/** Per-item base value: a single item's premium, before block discounts. */\nfunction itemBaseValue(item: Item): number {\n  return isComponent(item.type) ? COMPONENT_BASE : BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n}\n\n/** Per-item insurance value (block discounts do not change the insurance sum). */\nfunction itemInsuranceValue(item: Item): number {\n  return isComponent(item.type) ? COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE : INSURANCE_VALUE[item.type] ?? 0;\n}\n\n/** Total insured value of a list of items (cap = CAP_MULTIPLIER * this). */\nfunction insuranceSum(items: Item[]): number {\n  return items.reduce((sum, it) => sum + itemInsuranceValue(it), 0);\n}\n\n/** Item-specific risk surcharges (cursed, high enchantment). Applied to the affected item's base premium. */\nfunction itemSurcharges(item: Item): number {\n  const base = itemBaseValue(item);\n  let surcharge = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) surcharge += CURSE_RATE * base;\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANT_THRESHOLD) surcharge += HIGH_ENCHANT_RATE * base;\n  return surcharge;\n}\n\n/** Input shape for `runScenario`: a single customer and a list of steps. */\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype Incident = { cause: string; damages: Damage[] };\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items?: Item[] };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: Incident };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\ntype Scenario = { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }; steps: Step[] };\n\n/** A policy created by a quote: its insured items and the remaining payout cap. */\ntype Policy = { items: Item[]; remainingCap: number };\n\n/** Reimbursement rate for a damaged item: 50% if highly enchanted (>= 8), else full. */\nfunction reimbursementRate(item: Item): number {\n  return (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD\n    ? HIGH_ENCHANT_CLAIM_RATE\n    : 1;\n}\n\n/** Process a claim against a policy, mutating its remaining cap. */\nfunction processClaim(policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult {\n  const pool = [...policy.items];\n  let desired = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const index = pool.findIndex((it) => it.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (index === -1) {\n      throw new Error(`damage references item not covered by policy: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    }\n    const [item] = pool.splice(index, 1);\n    desired += reimbursementRate(item) * damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE;\n  }\n  const payout = roundDown(Math.min(desired, policy.remainingCap));\n  policy.remainingCap -= payout;\n  return { payout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap };\n}\n\n/** Total premium for a quote, applying item-specific and policy-wide modifiers plus the fee. */\nfunction quotePremium(\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number },\n  items: Item[],\n  isFollowUp: boolean,\n): number {\n  const policyBase = policyBasePremium(items);\n  const surcharges = items.reduce((sum, it) => sum + itemSurcharges(it), 0);\n  const firstInsurance = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD ? LOYALTY_RATE * policyBase : 0;\n  const followUpDiscount = isFollowUp ? FOLLOW_UP_RATE * policyBase : 0;\n  return roundUp(\n    policyBase + surcharges + firstInsurance - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE,\n  );\n}\n\nexport function runScenario(input: unknown): { results: StepResult[] } {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies = new Map<number, Policy>();\n  let hasPriorQuote = false;\n  scenario.steps.forEach((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      results.push({ premium: quotePremium(scenario.customer, items, hasPriorQuote) });\n      hasPriorQuote = true;\n      policies.set(index, { items, remainingCap: CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSum(items) });\n    } else {\n      const policy = policies.get(step.policy);\n      if (!policy) throw new Error(`claim references unknown policy: ${step.policy}`);\n      results.push(processClaim(policy, step.incident));\n    }\n  });\n  return { results };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784953056212},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ef9554dd4f47463a82b21202","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { resolve } from \"node:path\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./office.js\";\n\n/** Run the CLI as a subprocess, feeding `input` as stdin JSON. */\nfunction runCli(input: unknown): { stdout: string; stderr: string; exitCode: number } {\n  const cliPath = resolve(process.cwd(), \"src/cli.ts\");\n  const bin = resolve(process.cwd(), \"node_modules/.bin/tsx\");\n  try {\n    const stdout = execFileSync(bin, [cliPath], {\n      input: JSON.stringify(input),\n      encoding: \"utf-8\",\n      timeout: 30000,\n    });\n    return { stdout, stderr: \"\", exitCode: 0 };\n  } catch (err) {\n    const e = err as { stdout?: string; stderr?: string; status?: number };\n    return {\n      stdout: e.stdout ?? \"\",\n      stderr: e.stderr ?? \"\",\n      exitCode: e.status ?? 1,\n    };\n  }\n}\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  it(\"quote: empty item list -> premium 5 (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single sword -> premium 115\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single amulet -> premium 71\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single staff -> premium 93\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 93 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: single potion -> premium 49\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 49 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: 2 runes -> premium 60\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: 3 runes (block applies) -> premium 71\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: 4 runes (no block) -> premium 115\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: 7 runes -> premium 198 (ceil 197.5)\", () => {\n    const runes = Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" }));\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: runes }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: 2 runes + 1 moonstone (no block) -> premium 88 (ceil 87.5)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 88 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: 3 runes + 3 moonstones (two blocks) -> premium 137\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 137 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: cursed sword newcomer -> premium 165\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: high-enchanted sword enchant 5 -> premium 145\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }] },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: sword enchant 4 (no high enchant) -> premium 115\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4, cursed: false }] },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: cursed sword enchant 5 (both surcharges) -> premium 195\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 195 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: loyalty at exactly 2 years -> premium 95\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 95 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: follow-up contract (2nd quote) sword -> 1st 115, 2nd 100\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }, { premium: 100 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: cursed sword + plain amulet scope -> premium 231\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true },\n            { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 1, cursed: false },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 231 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"quote: long-standing 2nd contract cursed enchant 7 -> 1st 95, 2nd 160\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }] },\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 95 }, { premium: 160 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"claim: standard sword enchant 3 damage 500 -> payout 400, cap 1600\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({\n      results: [{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }],\n    });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"claim: rune damage 200 -> payout 100, cap 400\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: dragon sword enchant 8 damage 1000 -> payout 400, cap 1600\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: dragon sword enchant 9 damage 1000 -> payout 400\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: dragon sword enchant 5 damage 800 -> payout 700\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: steel sword enchant 9 damage 1000 -> payout 400\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: deductible per event sword+amulet 500+300 -> payout 600, cap 2600\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: two swords both damaged 500+300 -> payout 600, cap 3400\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: cap exhaustion two claims of 1500 -> 1400 then 600, caps 600 then 0\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: cursed sword huge damage -> payout 2000 (cap unmodified), cap 0\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: sword + 3 runes block huge damage -> payout 3500, cap 0\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: sword + amulet huge damage -> payout 3200, cap 0\");\n  it.todo(\"claim: payout rounding down enchant 8 damage 901 -> payout 350, cap 1650\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI: schema example happy path -> premium 59, payout 100, cap 1100, exit 0\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI: unknown item type in quote -> exit non-zero, stderr, no stdout\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI: claim damage for item not in policy -> exit non-zero\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI: claim damage with unknown item type -> exit non-zero\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI: claim damage with negative amount -> exit non-zero\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI: more damages of a type than insured -> exit non-zero\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784953056213},{"role":"assistant","content":[],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"error","timestamp":1784953056213,"errorMessage":"Request timed out."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","think