   - Subtotal: 8\n9. `throw new Error(`damage references item not covered by policy: ${damage.itemType}`);`\n   - conditional (throw) = 4\n   - `new Error` invocation = 2\n   - constant = 1\n   - `damage` binding = 1\n   - Subtotal: 8\n10. `const [item] = pool.splice(index, 1);`\n    - binding `item` = 1\n    - assignment = 6\n    - `pool.splice` invocation = 2\n    - `index` binding = 1\n    - `1` constant = 1\n    - Subtotal: 11\n11. `uncappedPayout += reimbursementRate(item) * damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE;`\n    - assignment (`+=`) = 6\n    - `reimbursementRate` invocation = 2\n    - `item` binding = 1\n    - `*` invocation = 2\n    - `damage` binding = 1\n    - `-` invocation = 2\n    - `DEDUCTIBLE` binding = 1\n    - Subtotal: 15\n12. `const payout = roundDown(Math.min(uncappedPayout, policy.remainingCap));`\n    - binding `payout` = 1\n    - assignment = 6\n    - `roundDown` invocation = 2\n    - `Math.min` invocation = 2\n    - `uncappedPayout` binding = 1\n    - `policy` binding = 1\n    - Subtotal: 13\n13. `policy.remainingCap -= payout;`\n    - assignment = 6\n    - `policy` binding = 1\n    - `payout` binding = 1\n    - Subtotal: 8\n14. `return { payout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap };`\n    - `payout` binding = 1\n    - `remainingCap` — key, treat as constant? = 1\n    - `policy` binding = 1\n    - Subtotal: 3\n\nHmm this is getting really tedious and the APP counting is quite subjective (property accesses, throws, array literals). Let me take a more principled, simpler counting that's defensible and consistent.\n\nLet me define clearly:\n- **Constant (1)**: literal values (`0`, `1`, `-1`, string literals)\n- **Binding (1)**: variables/params referenced (`policy`, `incident`, `pool`, `damage`, `index`, `item`, `payout`, `uncappedPayout`, `it`, `DEDUCTIBLE`)\n- **Invocation (2)**: function/method calls including operators used as functions? No — operators (`<`, `===`, `*`, `-`, `+=`) — APP lists \"Invocation (Mass 2): Function calls (`calculate()`, `Ma